  "problem": "Which of the following statements are true when testing the stability of Euler's method on the test equation ${y}^{\u2032}=-\\lambda y$ with $y=y(x),\\,y(0)=\\frac{3}{2},\\,x\\ge 0,\\,\\lambda =\\frac{9}{4},$ and step size $\u0394x?$  \n\n- The update formula can be written as ${y}_{n+1}=(1-\\frac{9}{4}\u0394x){y}_{n}.$\n- The method is stable for $|1-\\frac{9}{4}\u0394x|<1.$\n- The method is stable for step size $\u0394x=0.2.$\n- The method is **unstable** for step size $\u0394x=0.6.$",
